# Dashboard Server Actions

`lib/safe-action` creates one public client and two Better Auth clients. The adapter loads the session; `authorize` throws our errors — it does not call Next `unauthorized()` / `forbidden()`. `handleServerError` logs, then does that.

Every action sets metadata `{ actionName }` only.

- Public (sign-in, sign-out): `actionClient`
- Signed-in Staff or Owner: `staffActionClient` — missing User throws `UnauthorizedError`
- Owner-only: `ownerActionClient` — Staff throws `ForbiddenError`

Put Zod in `lib/validation`. Throw `utils/errors`. Dashboard forms: react-hook-form + Zod + `useAction`.

```ts
// ✅
export const signInAction = actionClient
  .metadata({ actionName: "signIn" })
  .inputSchema(signInSchema)
  .action(async ({ parsedInput }) => { /* ... */ });

// ❌ role in metadata; calling unauthorized() inside the action
.metadata({ actionName: "signIn", requiredRole: "admin" })
```
